13. Tests and acceptance criteria
Functional
•	☐ A 100-MPN upload searches each unique normalized key once in the turn, subject to explicit refresh/provider retry behavior, and saves all cacheable outcomes.
•	☐ A follow-up for five valid cached MPNs makes zero web searches and sends only those five results to the LLM.
•	☐ A mixed cached/new request searches only missing, expired, malformed, old-version, or bypassed keys.
•	☐ The same MPN in a different chat does not reuse the first chat's cache.
•	☐ Duplicate MPNs are searched once after normalization and map back to original Excel rows.
•	☐ ABC-123 and ABC123 remain distinct keys.
•	☐ All alternatives from the existing search pipeline are retained; no max-five truncation occurs.
•	☐ Expired/malformed/old-version entries are treated as misses.
•	☐ Genuine empty results are cached as no_alternatives; timeout/429/5xx are not.
•	☐ Successful force-refresh replaces the entry; failed refresh preserves the old entry and reports failure.
Compatibility/reliability
•	☐ Existing state fields survive mutation and the normal end-of-turn save.
•	☐ Cache survives end-of-turn save without a separate UPDATE.
•	☐ LLM prompt never includes the whole cache.
•	☐ Missing/corrupt webref does not break the turn.
•	☐ Concurrent same-chat requests cannot silently overwrite newer state.
•	☐ State size and load/save latency are measured before and after 100-MPN test.
•	☐ Tests include one or more MPNs with many alternatives.
