15. Instructions for Copilot
First inspect the repository; do not assume function names or architecture. Identify the conversation context model/repository, context serialization, end-of-turn save, MPN extraction, web-search function, and LLM prompt builder. Reuse existing project patterns and make the smallest safe changes.
•	Do not create a database table, migration, or independent cache save path.
•	Do not truncate alternatives to five or add a new per-MPN maximum.
•	Do not change unrelated state fields or schema_version without evidence it is required.
•	Do not send the full cache to the LLM.
•	Do not save search failures as no_alternatives.
•	Do not silently ignore concurrency conflicts.
•	Run relevant tests and report actual outcomes; do not claim tests passed unless they were executed.
At completion, report: files changed; where webref is stored; how hit/miss and TTL work; confirmation that no max-five cap exists; tests added/run and results; assumptions requiring confirmation; and any remaining concurrency limitations.
16. Final specification
Use the existing conversation_context row and store cache data at inner_state['webref']['alternatives'], keyed by normalized MPN (or manufacturer+MPN when required). Scope cache access to chat_id and validate user ownership. Cache successful results and genuine no-alternatives outcomes with per-entry result version and expiry. Preserve every alternative returned by the existing pipeline; do not add a max-five rule. Search only misses, merge once in memory, pass only requested current-turn results to the LLM, and persist using the existing end-of-turn save.
